{
  "mn19:0.1": "Middle Discourses 19 ",
  "mn19:0.2": "Two Kinds of Thought ",
  "mn19:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn19:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn19:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn19:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn19:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn19:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn19:2.1": "“Mendicants, before my awakening—when I was still unawakened but intent on awakening—I thought: ",
  "mn19:2.2": "‘Why don’t I meditate by continually dividing my thoughts into two classes?’ ",
  "mn19:2.3": "So I assigned sensual, malicious, and cruel thoughts ",
  "mn19:2.4": "to one class. ",
  "mn19:2.5": "And I assigned thoughts of renunciation, good will, and harmlessness ",
  "mn19:2.6": "to the second class. ",
  "mn19:3.1": "Then, as I meditated—diligent, keen, and resolute—a sensual thought arose. ",
  "mn19:3.2": "I understood: ",
  "mn19:3.3": "‘This sensual thought has arisen in me. ",
  "mn19:3.4": "It leads to hurting myself, hurting others, and hurting both. It blocks wisdom, it’s on the side of distress, and it doesn’t lead to extinguishment.’ ",
  "mn19:3.5": "When I reflected that it leads to hurting myself, it went away. ",
  "mn19:3.6": "When I reflected that it leads to hurting others, it went away. ",
  "mn19:3.7": "When I reflected that it leads to hurting both, it went away. ",
  "mn19:3.8": "When I reflected that it blocks wisdo